    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/assistant-director-of-athletic-events-operations-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Full-time regular 5734 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations; Athletics\n\n\nPosting # 5734 Department Description:\nAs part of the University of San Diego, a Roman Catholic University, the Department of Intercollegiate Athletics is committed to advancing academic and athletic excellence and enhancing students' lives while promoting the University of San Diego.\n\n\nUniversity Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. The Assistant Director designs and manages athletics event communications and marketing and works collaboratively with internal and external partners to ensure successful event execution.  The position also contributes to the Athletic Department’s external event solicitation efforts and sport-specific alumni engagement initiatives, including alumni nights, reunions, and team-related events. Duties and Responsibilities: Athletic Event Management & Hospitality Execution Independently plan, coordinate, and execute all athletic development events, managing end-to-end event logistics including theme concepts, invitation coordination, registration set up, attendance tracking venue selection, run-of-show timelines, staffing, and on-site leadership. Collaborate seamlessly with facilities, game operations, marketing, communications, ticketing, security, concessions, catering, and campus partners to ensure successful event execution. Design and produce compelling event invitations and digital communication materials using various creative platforms (e.g., Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva, ThankView).. Manage external event vendors, caterers, venues arrangements, rentals, décor, transportation, entertainment, and other external service providers. Oversee hospitality experiences associated with home athletics competitions, development events, donor receptions, VIP events, special events, and other high-profile athletics activities Coordinate the planning and execution of premium and VIP hospitality experiences, including hospitality suites, clubs, lounges, receptions, pre-game and post-game events, and other designated premium areas. Work athletic and donor events on weeknights and weekends when needed. Recruit, train, and manage event-day staffing, hospitality personnel, volunteers, student workers, and other event support as appropriate. Develop comprehensive hospitality plans covering guest lists, invitations, RSVPs, seating assignments, catering, décor, entertainment, staffing, credentials, parking, transportation, signage, and other event logistics Establish and track key event success metrics (attendance, engagement pipelines, revenue) and conducts post event assessments for continuous quality improvement. Serve as primary liaison to University Advancement and other campus departments for collaborative special events. Track event-related invoices, purchase orders, vendor payments, reimbursements, deposits, and revenue associated with development and hospitality activities. Monitor, review, and reconcile event budgets, expenditures, and gift accounts to ensure compliance and accuracy. Ensure all event operations, vendor contracts, insurance requirements, and hospitality activities comply with institutional policies, NCAA regulations, and conference standards. Alumni Engagement Identity and cultivate opportunities to engage donors, alumni and prospective supporters through external events and community-based activities Support sport team operations and special projects as assigned by the Senior Associate Athletic Director. Lead planning and execution of sport-specific alumni events, including alumni nights, reunions, and engagement activities for former student-athletes and supporters of individual sports programs. Collaborate with coaches, sport administrators, alumni relations, Athletics Development, and other campus partners to develop meaningful alumni engagement experiences connected to home games, competitions, special events, and team milestones. Assist with other team-specific engagement initiatives and special events as assigned. Facility Rentals and Administrative Operations Partner with the athletics facilities unit to solicit, coordinate, and finalize facility contracts for external events and rental clients. Formulate strategic recommendations for senior administration regarding external facility rentals to drive revenue growth and enhance  community outreach. Maintain master event calendars, operational schedules, production timelines, and critical department timelines. Maintain confidentiality and exercise sound judgment when handling sensitive financial, personnel, donor, and departmental information. Ensure event, hospitality, purchasing, and financial activities comply with applicable institutional policies, NCAA regulations, conference requirements, and other governing standards. Track project deliverables, maintain meeting documentation, and execute operational follow-up tasks. Perform other related duties and special projects as assigned. Special Conditions of Employment: Must work at all major fundraising events, Must be able and willing to work nights and/or weekends. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. Substitution: A high school diploma plus two additional years of work experience may substitute for degree requirement, at the rate of two years of higher education is equivalent to one year of work experience. Minimum one year of experience in events, athletic development, hospitality, higher education, or a related field required. Substitution: Master’s degree may substitute for 1 year of work experience. A commitment to quality, client and colleague-oriented service; tact and discretion in maintaining confidentiality with campus administrators, trustees, or donors. Preferred Qualifications: Experience within NCAA Division I intercollegiate athletics and/or university advancement preferred. Playing experience or participation in intercollegiate athletics preferred. Previous experience and working proficiency with event software, ThankView, Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva, Advance/Affinaquest, Workday, and Concur preferred. Performance Expectations - Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong oral and written communication skills; exceptional critical listening and editing abilities. Command of standard English grammar, spelling, punctuation, syntax, and proofreading skills. Strong teamwork and organizational skills with the ability to manage event staff and student teams effectively. Effective strategic thinking, creative problem-solving, meticulous attention to detail, and proactive initiative. Excellent organizational, project management, and time management skills; ability to manage multiple projects and events simultaneously. Flexibility and versatility to respond calmly to high-pressure situations and rapidly shifting event priorities. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint) and Google applications; ability to master new software platforms rapidly. Excellent interpersonal skills to interact and work with a broad range of people using tact and diplomacy Commitment to high-quality, client-oriented service, cultural competency, and absolute discretion regarding confidential information. Ability to work tactfully and diplomatically with all levels of USD constituents, including donors, trustees, alumni, administrators, vendors, and the public. Must display initiative and the ability to meet deadlines without supervision Maintain confidentiality of information regarding students and employees as required by University policy and the Buckley Amendment Maintain confidentiality of information regarding constituents, volunteers, and donors Posting Salary: $5,858.67-$6,000 per month; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Resume and Cover Letter Required Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application. In addition, please upload a cover letter and resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.  If you have any questions or difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: Hours: 40 hours per week Closing date: Open until filled Note : External job postings will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 93bbd92b Last Name (required) e6dab500 Email (required) 52e5fa79 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sponsored Programs Administrator San Diego, California Administrator, Office of the Vice President and Provost The Sponsored Programs Administrator, under the general direction of the Director, collaborates with faculty and staff in preparing and submitting federal, state and private grant and contract proposals. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert c39281ac Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrator Athletics Administrator Athletics Employment Type Full-time regular Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 7667eac8 Last Name (required) d301d1d0 Email (required) 02906a6a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/sponsored-programs-administrator-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Sponsored Programs Administrator",
      "description": "Sponsored Programs Administrator - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Sponsored Programs Administrator San Diego, California Full-time regular 5728 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Sponsored Programs Administrator: Sponsored Programs \n\n\nPosting # 5728 Department Description: The Office of Sponsored Programs at University of San Diego provides quality service and support to the USD community. Our team partners with faculty, administrators, and graduate students, assisting them from initial proposal development and budget preparation, to the submission of innovative, high quality, competitive proposals. After an award, OSP collaborates with internal and external partners to support the non-financial administration of the award, culminating in the project closeout. We are committed to advancing academic excellence by facilitating and sustaining a growing research enterprise. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: Join a mission-driven, dedicated team that partners with dynamic PIs across disciplines to advance innovative research and support projects that make a meaningful impact. As a Carnegie R2 institution with a growing research portfolio, USD offers an exciting opportunity for colleagues who are passionate about research administration, committed to our mission, and eager to grow with us. The Sponsored Programs Administrator, under the general direction of the Director, collaborates with faculty and staff in preparing and submitting federal, state and private grant and contract proposals. This position is responsible for the management of pre-award and non-financial post-award services for sponsored project agreements, including the review and negotiation of standard award terms. The Sponsored Programs Administrator will have strong analytic and deductive reasoning skills, the ability to manage multiple concurrent proposal deadlines under pressure while working independently and as part of a team, attention to detail across work of varying complexity, clear written and verbal communication with faculty and central office partners, and a commitment to a client-centered environment. Duties and Responsibilities: Contract and Grant Administration: Pre-Award activities: Work will support disciplines across campus as needed. Partner with PI and Co-PI eligible faculty and administrative investigators to develop and prepare complex research proposals, including budgets, budget justifications, administrative documents, and supporting materials. Advise and collaborate with faculty, administrators and staff to develop competitive proposals for external funds. Recommend specific grant programs and funding opportunities as appropriate to faculty, administrators and staff. Actively communicate with members of the campus community to remain engaged with and aware of interests and funding needs; work in cooperation with faculty, administrators and staff to develop interest in externally-funded research opportunities. Provide advice and assistance to faculty and staff during the development of grant, cooperative agreement, contract and subcontract proposals to for-profit, non-profit, federal, state and local government sponsors (e.g., interpreting federal and state regulations and University policy, sponsors’ proposal instructions and policies.) Create multi-year budgets for proposal submission, ensuring regulations such as applicable direct and indirect costs, subcontracts, travel, and fringe benefit rates are followed while conforming to proposal guidelines established by external funding agencies and institutional policies and procedures. Submits proposals through various electronic systems including, but not limited to, Cayuse Proposals (S2S), Research.gov, Grants.gov, and other systems. Inform departmental budget managers and/or deans of required mandatory cost-share and course reassigned time to be paid by research grants and contracts. Respond to external agency requests related to proposal submissions and/or revisions in a timely manner. Coordinates with external organizations and institutions on collaborative submissions, as needed. Advising faculty and administrators regarding institutional policies for biohazards, animal use, human subjects, required matching funds, and sub-contractors on externally funded proposals and providing guidance for regarding compliance forms per sponsor or USD requirements. Secure the concurrence of the Principal Investigator and other University offices, as appropriate, prior to accepting awards with non-standard terms and conditions. Advise all concerned parties of their responsibilities in meeting special or unusual award requirements. Investigates and maintains a strong knowledge of federal, state, and local government rules and regulations that govern research grants and contracts and stays informed on sponsored terms and conditions for submitting and negotiating grant awards. Post-Award activities: Analyzes, coordinates, approves, and submits requests for prior approval of post award changes and actions to external sponsors/agencies. Utilize information in Cayuse to provide funding and other analysis reports for research/grant topics as requested by departmental budget managers and/or deans offices. Interpret sponsor approval requirements, policies, federal regulations, state statues and University policy related to the management and administration of extramural awards. Work collaboratively with Grants Accounting to resolve issues related to post-award financial terms and conditions. Assist PIs, staff and administrators with project administrative concerns, inquiries, or issues to ensure compliance with sponsor and University policies and best practices. General Management: Lead pre-award to post-award transition meetings between project stakeholders including Sponsored Programs, Grants Accounting, project personnel, budget administrators, and others as needed. Maintain regular contact and strong working relationship with other university departments and offices, and with faculty, administrators, staff, and outside funding agencies to facilitate the effective administration of the university’s externally funded programs and opportunities for such. Examples of such departments and offices include but are not limited to the Controller’s Office, Payroll, Human Resources, Foundation Relations, Procurement, Public Affairs, and the Office of the General Counsel. Provide information on award terms and proposal information for pre-award to post-award transition meetings between project stakeholders including Sponsored Programs, Grants Accounting, project personnel, budget administrators, and others as needed. Other Responsibilities Assists in writing and editing office documents and reports as required. Contributes to office team building efforts. Participates in professional development to continuously develop existing knowledge and expertise in all aspects of research administration. Participates in training and advising of faculty, administrators, staff and students on proposal development and grant management through one-on-one meetings or collaborative sessions. Assists with faculty training workshops upon request. Certificates, Licenses, Registrations: Certified Research Administrator (CRA) certification is desirable. Special Conditions of Employment: While this is a full-time, off-campus position, candidates must live in the San Diego County or the greater region, as the position will require in-person meetings and on campus work on a consistent basis. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university required. Three or more years of experience required in sponsored research administration. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited college or university in business or finance related area preferred. Five or more years of experience in sponsored research administration preferred. Training in electronic research administration (Cayuse Research Suite) and financial/HR database (Workday) preferred; incumbent will be trained if needed. Performance Expectations - Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge: Excellent mathematical and analytical skills Excellent verbal and written communication skills Demonstrated ability to meet deadlines and work with details; time management skills Advanced knowledge and understanding of concepts, policies and procedures, and Regulatory requirements associated with the development, implementation and administration of scientific research projects including but not limited to: Uniform Guidance; CFR; EDGAR; FAR; IRS; USD Policies and Procedures; General Accounting Best Practices. Advanced knowledge of project budgeting and fiscal management. Advanced knowledge of the structure, operations and requirements of federal, state and local financial regulatory and funding agencies. Comprehensive knowledge and understanding of research pre-and post-award procedures and requirements. Advanced knowledge and demonstrated proficiency in electronic research administration, including database applications, spreadsheet development and electronic document preparation. Experience in proposal submission, and in review/negotiation of contracts, subcontracts, and other agreements. Knowledge of contract frameworks, legal liability mitigation, and complex regulatory compliance policies. Skills: Skill in examining and re-engineering operations and procedures, formulating processes, and developing and implementing new strategies and procedures. Strong analytical, problem solving, and critical thinking skills. Demonstrated leadership, organizational and management skills. Project management skills and the ability to resolve complex problems and issues. Strong consultative and advisory skills. Skill in developing and conducting employee compliance training/orientation sessions. Skill in developing university policy and procedure documentation. Demonstrated negotiating skills. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a collaborative/diverse community. Highly developed communication skills, both verbal and written. Attention to detail. Abilities: Ability to make complex administrative/procedure decisions and judgments under pressure and prioritize tight proposal deadlines. Ability to create, review, negotiate, and modify contracts. Ability to develop and present educational programs and/or workshops. Ability to foster a cooperative work environment. Ability to develop and maintain record-keeping systems and procedures. Ability to analyze budgetary line items for compliance with budget guidelines. Ability to manage a large volume of projects with concurrent deadlines, work independently and use sound business practices to accomplish objectives. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to exercise independent judgment. Posting Salary: $5,859-$6,166 per month; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Resume and Cover Letter Required Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application. In addition, please upload a cover letter and resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.  If you have any questions or difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: Hours: 37.5 Closing date: Open until filled Note : External job postings will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 1f8652a4 Last Name (required) 2eb12d06 Email (required) 5778e157 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b0c4e895 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrator Office of the Vice President and Provost Administrator Office of the Vice President and Provost Employment Type Full-time regular Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 701a1299 Last Name (required) cc9d2d28 Email (required) e9796565 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/open-rank-assistant-associate-or-full-professor-of-english-and-writing-program-director-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Open Rank (Assistant, Associate or Full) Professor of English and Writing Program Director",
      "description": "Open Rank (Assistant, Associate or Full) Professor of English and Writing Program Director - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Open Rank (Assistant, Associate or Full) Professor of English and Writing Program Director San Diego, California Faculty Full-time regular Closing on: Nov 1 2026 5668 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Open Rank (Assistant, Associate or Full) Professor of English and Writing Program Director\n\n\nPosting # 5668 Department Description: The Department of English at the University of San Diego, housed within the College of Artsand Sciences, is a multidisciplinary Department that features courses in domestic and global literatures, literary cultures and theories, and creative writing. The Department also houses the University’s First Year Writing Program. The College of Arts and Sciences is at the heart of the University of San Diego. Our philosophy is built on the enduring values of the Catholic intellectual tradition, immersing students in the concepts of free inquiry, ethical conduct and compassionate service. The College aims to establish an academic foundation for students to thrive and gain a comprehensive education, which spans the sciences, arts and social sciences. Through our exemplary liberal arts education and rigorous scholarship, we aspire to not only educate the mind but also develop the whole person. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Department of English at the University of San Diego invites applications for the position of Director of the University Writing Program to begin in Fall of 2027. We seek applicants at the level of advanced assistant, associate, or full professor of English. The teaching assignment is four courses per year. Teaching responsibilities include writing and literature courses at all levels. Administrative responsibilities include collaboration with faculty and administration in overseeing USD’s Writing Program; supervision of first-year writing courses; contributing to personnel decisions (in consultation with English department chair); incoming student assessment and competency exams; coordinating all upper division, cross-curricular writing courses, including training faculty, reviewing Core Advanced Writing-course applications and syllabi; offering training workshops for all Writing Program faculty; Writing Program assessment; oversight of English for Speakers of Other Languages student assessment and support programming. Job Requirements: The successful candidate will be a writing specialist with a PhD in English, Rhetoric and Composition, or a related field, with meaningful preparation in English literature preferred, and an interest in Creative Writing welcome. Substantial experience in Writing Program leadership administration, background in working with Writing Across the Curriculum and Writing in the Disciplines; Writing Program assessment; Writing Centers; and English for Speakers of Other Languages programs also required. Significant record of publication and research in the field expected. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Posting salary: $6,931.25-$11,666.67 monthly: Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Please submit all materials by Sunday, October 4, 2026 Application materials must include: A cover letter of application, which should express: A philosophy of writing pedagogy (particularly in an age of GenAI), including concrete examples of the ways that those principles have been implemented in teaching, research, and writing program administration. The candidate’s plans for service, commitment to the University mission, and inclusivity in teaching, research, and Writing Program Administration. Curriculum Vitae Research statement and sample of scholarly or, if applicable, creative work Teaching statement and sample syllabi that indicate an ability and willingness to teach reading and writing as twinned skills, as well as a discussion of the candidate’s commitment to inclusive pedagogy A one-page statement of vision for the writing program at USD Contact information for three references who will be sent a link to upload letters. Please contact Professor Brad Melekian, English Department Chair and Search Committee Chair, with any questions, at melekian@sandiego.edu . If you have any technical difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) f857d6d6 Last Name (required) b4d32053 Email (required) fae730ce Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 1f8d04c0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts and Sciences Faculty College of Arts and Sciences Faculty Employment Type Faculty Full-time regular Faculty Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 726c6af3 Last Name (required) 6568ea1c Email (required) 8d1b67b9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
