    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-theatre-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Theatre",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Theatre - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Assistant Professor, Theatre San Diego, California Full-time regular 5697 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Assistant Professor, Theatre\n\n\nPosting # 5697 Department Description: The Department of Theatre offers a Bachelor of Arts program dedicated to developing well-rounded student artists who are prepared to shape a vibrant, culturally rich theatrical landscape. We believe students learn best by doing. Through hands-on practice, we foster an environment where students are empowered to experiment, take creative risks, and grow from every experience. The College of Arts and Sciences is at the heart of the University of San Diego. Our philosophy is built on the enduring values of the Catholic intellectual tradition, immersing students in the concepts of free inquiry, ethical conduct and compassionate service. The College aims to establish an academic foundation for students to thrive and gain a comprehensive education, which spans the sciences, arts and social sciences. Through our exemplary liberal arts education and rigorous scholarship, we aspire to not only educate the mind but also develop the whole person. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Theatre Department at the University of San Diego invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Theatre Studies. We are looking for a teacher-scholar who is as passionate about the \"how\" of teaching as they are about the \"what\" of their research. Our department operates with a 3-3 teaching load , focusing on a mix of lower-division introductory courses and more focused upper-division classes. While we value and support active scholarship, excellence in the classroom is our highest priority. If you thrive on mentoring students and sparking a deep appreciation for the stage across centuries and cultures, you’ll find a home here. The successful candidate will lead courses in: ● Theatre History ● Performance Studies ● Script Analysis We are particularly interested in candidates whose research and experience extend beyond the traditions of the United States and Western Europe and who may further develop our curriculum to include the global breadth of performance. Other duties may include supporting departmental shows by serving as Dramaturg or Director, depending on skill-set. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: ● Ph.D. in Theatre, Performance Studies, or a related field (ABD considered if degree is completed by start date). ● Demonstrated record of teaching excellence. ● A research agenda that informs and enriches their classroom practice. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Posting Salary: $7,500-$7,917 monthly: Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: For full consideration, applications should be completed and submitted by October 2nd, 2026. 1. Cover Letter addressing qualifications and suitability for the position. 2. Curriculum Vitae. 3. Teaching Statement: (Max 1 page) Outlining your philosophy and classroom methods and approach to inclusive pedagogy. 4. Research Statement: (Max 1 page) Outlining your current projects and future goals. 5. Sample of Scholarly Work: (Article, book chapter, or conference paper). 6. Contact information for three professional references. Contact the Chair of the Department of Theatre, Nate Parde (nparde@sandiego.edu) with any questions. For technical questions or difficulties, contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 3d557e78 Last Name (required) d2643c51 Email (required) 0169a5e6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 891b3363 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts and Sciences Faculty College of Arts and Sciences Faculty Employment Type Full-time regular Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 2415f99a Last Name (required) 3fcbe0b9 Email (required) dec39692 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
