    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-electrical-engineering-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Electrical Engineering - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Adjunct Faculty, Electrical Engineering San Diego, California Faculty Part-time temporary 5532 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Adjunct Faculty, Electrical Engineering\n\n\nPosting # 5532 Department Description: The electrical engineering department at USD is part of the Shiley-Marcos School of Engineering (SMSE), which is ranked by U.S. News in the top 15 of non-doctoral engineering schools. The department offers undergraduate degrees in electrical engineering and consists of faculty who are devoted, challenging and inspiring students to learn the technical skills in electronics, embedded systems, power and communications. The mission of the school is to provide graduates with the perspective, social awareness and leadership skills necessary for becoming change making engineers. The department intends to introduce a new concentration in Intelligent Systems in the future. For more information about the Shiley-Marcos School of Engineering and the electrical engineering program, please visit : https://www.sandiego.edu/engineering/ University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Department of Electrical Engineering at the University of San Diego (USD) invites applications for a part-time teaching faculty to provide in person instruction to begin September 1, 2026. Candidates from all areas of specialization will be considered. Immediate instructional needs include but are not limited to: electromechanical systems, circuits, electrical power, and semiconductors. Special Conditions of Employment: Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: MS or PhD in Electrical Engineering or closely related field with a minimum of five years of experience in the industry or in academia (and candidates with a BS degree and ten years of experience, at least 3 of which are in teaching) Demonstrated teaching effectiveness at the college level, or evidence of strong teaching potential for candidates coming from industry Breadth of competency across core EE content areas appropriate for undergraduate instruction (circuits, electronics, signals and systems, embedded systems, etc.) Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching laboratory courses and supervising hands-on design projects Industry experience, particularly in product design, systems engineering, or applied EE Experience with or interest in capstone and senior design mentorship Familiarity with ABET accreditation processes and outcomes-based assessment Professional Engineer (PE) licensure or eligibility Experience mentoring undergraduate researchers or student competition teams Demonstrated commitment to inclusive pedagogy and teaching diverse student populations Posting Salary: $2,325 - $2,425 per unit The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application. In addition, please upload the following to your application profile for the hiring managers' review. Resume /Curriculum vitae. Application letter providing background and motivation not evident in the resume/CV. Courses in electrical engineering that can be taught by the candidate. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Contact: Paula Schmid, pschmid@sandiego.edu If you have any technical difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) a7aa95c2 Last Name (required) 25b6efbf Email (required) 8a5dd54d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Leadership Giving and Engagement San Diego, California Administrator, University Advancement The associate director of Leadership Giving and Engagement is responsible for increasing annual giving participation and activity from alumni, parents, and friends. In collaboration with the senior director of Donor Relations and Communications, the associate director initiates strategies to engage President’s Club prospects and move $500 annual donors to the President’s Club giving level ($1,500). Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Operations San Diego, California Administrator, Athletics The Assistant Director of Athletics Events & Operations serves as the primary operational and hospitality lead for athletic development events and hospitality experiences.  Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director of Finance and Administration, this role is responsible for developing, planning, coordinating, and executing high-impact athletics development events and hospitality experiences designed to enhance donor stewardship, elevate the USD Athletics brand, and cultivate relationships with donors, alumni, prospects, coaches, and other key constituents. Serving as a liaison to University Advancement embedded within Athletics, this position collaborates closely with internal and external partners to drive sport-specific alumni engagement, external facility rentals, and revenue-generating special events. Technology and Mobility Applications Analyst San Diego, California Administrator, Parking Services Reporting to the Director, University Mobility and Scheduling, the Technology and Mobility\nApplications Analyst is charged with overseeing Business Technology implementations and innovations related to parking and tram services and supporting scheduling applications for university wide event planning. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 9dd8f6bf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Shiley-Marcos School of Engineering Faculty Shiley-Marcos School of Engineering Employment Type Faculty Part-time temporary Faculty Part-time temporary Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 88051450 Last Name (required) 4884f3a5 Email (required) 408caf73 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
