e enduring values of the Catholic intellectual tradition, immersing students in the concepts of free inquiry, ethical conduct and compassionate service. The College aims to establish an academic foundation for students to thrive and gain a comprehensive education, which spans the sciences, arts and social sciences. Through our exemplary liberal arts education and rigorous scholarship, we aspire to not only educate the mind but also develop the whole person. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d4039ad3 Last Name (required) 80732af0 Email (required) dd1bfa17 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Director of Banquets and Catering San Diego, California Administrator, Dining Services The Assistant Director of Banquets and Catering is responsible for coordination and execution of the functional operation of the Banquets and Catering Department. The Assistant Director is responsible for the training, coordination, and evaluation of full-time and part-time office and service staff. Recreational Wellness Engagement Coordinator San Diego, California Administrator, Student Affairs The Engagement Coordinator is responsible for creating welcoming, meaningful, and inclusive opportunities that connect students to the University of San Diego community through Recreational Wellness. Serving as the primary steward of the Torero Engagement Lounge, this position oversees Esports programming, daily facility operations, student staffing, marketing initiatives, and student engagement strategies designed to foster belonging, holistic wellness, and lifelong healthy behaviors. Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator San Diego, California Facilities, Staff The Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator is responsible for assisting in the day-to-day coordination, operation, support, and updating of Facilities Management’s (FM) Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS), Preventive Maintenance (PM) Program, Deferred Maintenance (DM) Program, and the associated Reporting, Metrics and Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) of these programs and other systems in use in Facilities Management. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b6673577 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts and Sciences Faculty College of Arts and Sciences Faculty Employment Type Part-time temporary Part-time temporary Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) ab959975 Last Name (required) 41c4e23e Email (required) 85f7457f Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary f