    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/facilities-technology-and-data-coordinator-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator",
      "description": "Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator San Diego, California Full-time regular 5750 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator; Facilities Management Technology Posting # 5750 Department Description: The mission of the University of San Diego Facilities Management Department is to efficiently operate, maintain, and support the development of quality facilities, grounds, and services, and at the same time to support our campus community, students, faculty, and staff. Through our efforts we support the university's commitment to pursuing truth, academic excellence, and the advancement of knowledge. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: The Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator is responsible for assisting in the day-to-day coordination, operation, support, and updating of Facilities Management’s (FM) Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS), Preventive Maintenance (PM) Program, Deferred Maintenance (DM) Program, and the associated Reporting, Metrics and Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) of these programs and other systems in use in Facilities Management. CMMS duties and responsibilities include system administration tasks, gathering and verifying building, area and asset data, and the review of finished work orders for data integrity. Additional duties include mobile device application training, support, management, and troubleshooting. The PM Program responsibilities include the scheduling of preventive maintenance, ensuring a distributed workload across all trades and technicians. The coordinator will ensure that the program can rely on accurate assets, space, and task data. The DM Program responsibilities include gathering and tracking new and ongoing deferred maintenance projects. These projects typically include building systems and equipment that have recently been added or revised due to design, construction, and renovation. The coordinator will create and generate reports, KPI dashboards, metrics and analytics for these programs and others in use in Facilities Management. This position will be instrumental in process improvement. The evaluation of asset information, preventive maintenance schedule configuration and accurate finished work order information as Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator 8/12/2026 it relates to work force productivity will be critical. The coordinator will make recommendations to managers on methods of improvement. Special projects relating to other FM programs and systems may be assigned. Duties and Responsibilities: Program and System Administration: CMMS Administration Complete tasks such as asset and equipment management, user and access permissions changes, system and workflow testing, and troubleshooting. Review finished work orders for accurate recording of technician labor and comments. Train technicians in the use of CMMS mobile applications. Maintain inventory of all mobile devices. As business processes evolve, learn and implement new processes and train staff. Create reports, KPI dashboards, metrics and analytics to support FM operations. Assist the FM organization in striving toward a data centric business model. PM Program Responsible for scheduling planned work related to maintaining and operating the Facilities Management assets and infrastructure of the campus. Research, standardize and document preventive maintenance procedures for new equipment installations and for maintaining existing equipment. Coordinate with trades to establish schedules of preventative maintenance tasks and set up a continuous improvement process to ensure PMs are efficient. DM Program Responsible for maintaining lists of deferred maintenance equipment, systems, and projects. Coordinate with Planning, Design & Construction and Building & Grounds Operations to track and record finished work that affects the DM program. Data Gathering, Management and Analysis Collect, verify, and input data into the CMMS regarding building assets, equipment, systems, and areas. Organize, maintain, and keep current records of work performed, productivity and trends. Analyze requirements and performance measurements and develop reports to include cost trends, manpower performance and areas for improvement, to give management the data to make sound business decisions. Work with Business Technology Applications Manager to develop reports to track effort, inventory, work order backlog, completion, and efficiency. Process Improvement and Training Use a systematic approach to help Facilities Management optimize processes to achieve more efficient results. Proactively identify, analyze and recommend improvements to current workflow processes. Serve as steward of our processes, documenting current processes and creating processes. Certificates, Licenses, Registrations: Valid California driver’s license required. Special Conditions of Employment: Must be able to work assigned hours and may be required to work overtime and on weekends, as needed.  Work schedule may be adjusted to meet the demands of the department. Consistently follow safety practices appropriate to the job and comply with rules and regulations established by the University, state, and federal agencies. Job hours and/or workday may be changed when necessary to meet supervisory commitments. Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Job Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: High School diploma required. Minimum two years of related experience working with systems, technology, and/or equipment. Previous experience with record keeping / inventory control. Preferred Qualifications: Associate's degree is preferred in Information Systems, Facilities Management, Business Administration, or a closely related field. Two or more years of experience in a Facilities Management operation, preferably working with a CMMS system. Ability and experience in reading and understanding Architectural plans including HVAC, Mechanical, Electrical, Plumbing, and other consultant drawings. Familiarity with building equipment and systems including HVAC, Mechanical, Plumbing and Electrical. Experience creating visual charts, graphs, and metrics from complex data. Experience with coordinating and planning work, tracking progress, and completion. Performance Expectations - Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Strong attention to detail, thoroughness, and data quality. Significant skill or experience with TMA or other similar CMMS. Ability to input significant amounts of data into CMMS, spreadsheets, and other documents with attention to detail and speed required. Excellent verbal and written communication skills required. Excellent analytical and problem-solving skills required. Demonstrated ability to solve problems. Requires professional verbal and written correspondence, reports and recommendations to managers and supervisors, and daily interaction with superintendents and field staff. Ability to work with a diverse group in a positive and productive manner is required. Understands the importance of customer service and can follow-up as well as communicate to FM and campus clients. Other duties as assigned to support the overall operations of the department. Posting Salary: $25.36 - 28.90 per hour; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Resume Required Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application and, for full consideration, please upload a resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review.  If you have any questions or difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. Additional Details: Hours: 40 hours per week Closing date: Open until filled Note : External job postings will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 17044018 Last Name (required) 38a0401d Email (required) d9cf4a68 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Director of Banquets and Catering San Diego, California Administrator, Dining Services The Assistant Director of Banquets and Catering is responsible for coordination and execution of the functional operation of the Banquets and Catering Department. The Assistant Director is responsible for the training, coordination, and evaluation of full-time and part-time office and service staff. Recreational Wellness Engagement Coordinator San Diego, California Administrator, Student Affairs The Engagement Coordinator is responsible for creating welcoming, meaningful, and inclusive opportunities that connect students to the University of San Diego community through Recreational Wellness. Serving as the primary steward of the Torero Engagement Lounge, this position oversees Esports programming, daily facility operations, student staffing, marketing initiatives, and student engagement strategies designed to foster belonging, holistic wellness, and lifelong healthy behaviors. Assistant Professor of Marital and Family Therapy San Diego, California Faculty, School of Leadership and Education Sciences The Department of Counseling and Marital and Family Therapy at the University of San Diego invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position with a 9-month academic appointment beginning in Fall 2027 in the Marital and Family Therapy (MFT) program. Applicants will be considered for the faculty title of Assistant Professor. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f236d57c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Facilities Staff Facilities Staff Employment Type Full-time regular Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 8d875583 Last Name (required) 9b61b1ab Email (required) 94487661 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-marital-and-family-therapy-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Marital and Family Therapy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Marital and Family Therapy - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Assistant Professor of Marital and Family Therapy San Diego, California Faculty Full-time regular 5736 Add to favorites View favorites Position Title & Department: Assistant Professor of Marital and Family Therapy Posting # 5736 Department Description: The Department of Counseling and Marital and Family Therapy includes masters programs in Marital and Family Therapy (COAMFTE accredited), Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CACREP accredited), and School Counseling (CACREP accredited). The MFT program size is approximately 75 students. Students in the program pursue their degree full-time (two years) and many receive financial assistance. The program has developed strong collaborative relationships with local agencies to provide an array of practicum sites in the community. In addition, students are required to participate in at least one global education experience prior to graduation. University Description: The University of San Diego, an engaged and contemporary Catholic institution, was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Initially founded in 1962 as an education department within the College for Women, the School of Leadership and Education Sciences (SOLES) was officially established in 2005. As the second oldest academic institution at the University of San Diego (USD), the school has been shaped by a profound dedication to educational equity, which drives the mission and foundational values of SOLES and guides the school’s compassionate and strategic vision to help shape the future by educating and empowering professionals to enact academic justice, enhance human dignity and improve the quality of life across our  communities locally and globally. SOLES develops future leaders, educators, and mental health practitioners to be catalysts for change by offering unparalleled experiences and thought-provoking curricula. The school serves graduate students across three departments and offers three doctoral programs, nine master’s degrees, teacher credential programs, five undergraduate offerings, as well as seven certificates for graduate credit. SOLES is also home to eight centers and institutes that foster an ongoing commitment to assess regional needs and devise unique solutions; the initiatives the school has established and launched offer accessibility and opportunity while also confronting the challenges faced by underserved communities in the region. SOLES also maintains municipal and global partnerships, understanding that local action combined with global collaboration has the potential to inspire significant progress and change. Knowing that students gain the unique insight and perspectives necessary to thrive as global citizens by studying abroad, the school ensures all students fulfill an international requirement, providing a meaningful learning experience that complements the university’s liberal arts education. The School of Leadership and Education Sciences (SOLES) at the University of San Diego is recognized for its excellence and transformative contributions to education and leadership. A few key highlights that reflect SOLES’ unwavering commitment to community engagement, leadership, regional, transnational, and international impact.include: The only active Holmes Scholars Program in California supporting doctoral students in education. Eight centers and institutes including the Catholic Institute for Mental Health Ministry, Center for Restorative Justice, Character Education Resource Center, The Global Center, the Jacobs Institute, the Manchester Family Child Development Center, the Nonprofit Institute, and the newly launched Center for Embodied Equity and Neurodiversity. Bold InGenius Initiative advancingopportunity for marginalized communities through innovative leadership and collaboration. Johnson’s Fellows for Anti-Ablist Teaching supporting teachers in the San Diego region who wish to deepen their understanding of best teaching practices for supporting students with disabilities. SOLES develops and prepares the next generation of skilled practitioners to use their passion and knowledge to ignite meaningful change and embrace innovation. As a binational university situated on the border of San Diego and Mexico, we embrace our commitment to work directly with the demographics of the community we serve, including veteran and active military personnel, individuals across the socio-economic spectrum, and students from a wide array of ethnic and linguistic communities. The school’s faculty are recognized and respected experts in their field, committed to pedagogical quality and impactful  scholarship. Student success is thanks to not just faculty but also the administrators and staff, who are equally devoted to ensuring the SOLES community receives the resources and support services needed to succeed. In addition to WSCUC institutional accreditation, many of the school’s programs hold prestigious programmatic accreditations. The MA in Marital and Family Therapy has maintained accreditation with the Commission on Accreditation for Marriage and Family Therapy Education (COAMFTE) since 1992. The MA in Counseling, School Counseling, and Clinical Mental Health Counseling specializations have maintained accreditation with the Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs (CACREP) since 2007 and 2013, respectively. The School Counseling program has also been approved by the California Commission on Teacher Credentialing (CCTC) as a pathway for students to earn a California Pupil Personnel Services School Counseling credential. Likewise, the MEd in Curriculum and Instruction with Credentials is an approved educator preparation program by the CCTC. The MEd provides pathways for candidates to earn preliminary credentials in multiple subjects, single subjects, education specialist, and/or multiple subjects with bilingual authorization. Detailed Description: The Department of Counseling and Marital and Family Therapy at the University of San Diego invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position with a 9-month academic appointment beginning in Fall 2027 in the Marital and Family Therapy (MFT) program. Applicants will be considered for the faculty title of Assistant Professor. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful applicant will be expected to teach courses in the MFT Program, as well as supervise students through the practicum course. Faculty members are also expected to demonstrate scholarly productivity, as reflected in publications, professional presentations, and research grants. Additional responsibilities include but are not limited to student advising/mentoring, admissions, curriculum assessment and development, and general departmental, university, and national service. The successful applicant will 1) contribute to the department’s mission of providing outstanding teaching, research, and service; 2) collaborate productively with students and faculty at USD; and 3) have strong oral and written communication skills. Job Requirements: Required Qualifications: The faculty is seeking individuals who have demonstrated strong teaching skills and the ability to develop a coherent research agenda. Candidates for this position must meet the following minimum criteria: an earned doctorate in Marital and Family Therapy from a COAMFTE accredited program. ABD candidates will be considered, but must complete degree requirements by date of appointment demonstrated evidence of scholarly productivity (i.e., publications, presentations, and/or grant funding) evidence of strong, or potential for, graduate-level teaching evidence of strong, or potential for, relational/systemic clinical supervision AAMFT Approved Supervisor. Approved Supervisor Candidates will also be considered. California LMFT license eligible Preferred Qualification: Experience and interest in systemic family therapy with children and adolescents Background check: Successful completion of a pre-employment background check. Degree Verification Requirement : Persons offered employment in this position will be required to provide official education transcripts for degree verification purposes. Posting Salary: $8,313 - $10,159 Monthl; Excellent Benefits The University of San Diego offers a very competitive benefits package including; medical, dental, vision, a retirement contribution given to you by the University, and access to on-campus Fitness Centers.  Please visit the benefits section of our website to view all of the perks and benefits that USD has to offer. USD: Human Resources: Benefits The salary range provided in this posting reflects what we reasonably expect to pay for this position.  Actual compensation offered or earned is dependent on experience, education and other factors including departmental budget. Special Application Instructions: Applicants must submit: 1) cover letter that includes a summary of teaching and research experience and interests, 2) current curriculum vitae, 3) copies of two publications, 4) evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., course evaluations), and 5) contact information for three references Click the 'Apply Now' button to complete our online application and, for full consideration, please upload a resume to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review. If you have any questions, please contact the CMFT department Executive Assistant, Sheila Sosa at ssosa@sandiego.edu . If you have any technical difficulties please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu. We will begin reviewing applications on December 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received after December 1, 2026 may be reviewed depending on the progress of our search but are not guaranteed full consideration. Additional Details: This is a full-time, tenure-track nine-month faculty position with a competitive salary and comprehensive benefits package. The School of Leadership and Education Sciences at the University of San Diego is committed to serving our region’s dynamic demographics. We welcome candidates who share this commitment through their teaching, scholarship, and community engaged work. The University of San Diego is a smoking and tobacco-free campus. For more information, visit www.sandiego.edu/smokefree. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 6092ae9a Last Name (required) fceac22e Email (required) e5575b1c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Director of Banquets and Catering San Diego, California Administrator, Dining Services The Assistant Director of Banquets and Catering is responsible for coordination and execution of the functional operation of the Banquets and Catering Department. The Assistant Director is responsible for the training, coordination, and evaluation of full-time and part-time office and service staff. Recreational Wellness Engagement Coordinator San Diego, California Administrator, Student Affairs The Engagement Coordinator is responsible for creating welcoming, meaningful, and inclusive opportunities that connect students to the University of San Diego community through Recreational Wellness. Serving as the primary steward of the Torero Engagement Lounge, this position oversees Esports programming, daily facility operations, student staffing, marketing initiatives, and student engagement strategies designed to foster belonging, holistic wellness, and lifelong healthy behaviors. Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator San Diego, California Facilities, Staff The Facilities Technology and Data Coordinator is responsible for assisting in the day-to-day coordination, operation, support, and updating of Facilities Management’s (FM) Computerized Maintenance Management System (CMMS), Preventive Maintenance (PM) Program, Deferred Maintenance (DM) Program, and the associated Reporting, Metrics and Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) of these programs and other systems in use in Facilities Management. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b5287d8b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty School of Leadership and Education Sciences Faculty School of Leadership and Education Sciences Employment Type Faculty Full-time regular Faculty Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 8b36711b Last Name (required) f4fcaeb1 Email (required) c0ca0e5c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.sandiego.edu/jobs/provost-s-faculty-fellows-in-artificial-intelligence-two-san-diego-california-united-states": {
      "title": "Provost's Faculty Fellows in Artificial Intelligence (two)",
      "description": "Provost's Faculty Fellows in Artificial Intelligence (two) - San Diego, California, United States Skip to main content Why USD Benefits and Compensation Already Applied? My Profile Kiosk mode Employment Opportunities at USD Provost's Faculty Fellows in Artificial Intelligence (two) San Diego, California Faculty Full-time regular Closing on: Nov 15 2026 5756 Position Title & Department: Provost's Faculty Fellows in Artificial Intelligence (two) Posting # 5756 Department Description: The mission of Office of the Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs at USD is to provide academic leadership to its college and schools and promote excellence in all of the university's academic programs and initiatives, in order to educate ethical and compassionate leaders. University Description: The University of San Diego, a contemporary and engaged Roman Catholic institution , was founded by the Diocese of San Diego and the Society of the Sacred Heart in 1949. Governed by an independent board of trustees since 1972, USD remains committed to a liberal arts education grounded in the Catholic intellectual tradition and the pursuit of truth, goodness and beauty. Inspired by this centuries old tradition of Catholic higher education, the University welcomes people of all faith traditions and any, or no, religious background. The future success of USD relies on the contributions of those who seek to foster the development of engaged global citizens and an earnest confrontation of humanity’s urgent challenges . Detailed Description: This recruitment is open to current University of San Diego tenured faculty only. Two Provost's AI Faculty Fellows will work closely with the Provost's team focusing on designing strategies and implementing initiatives to support and advance the university's approach to AI in alignment with the Pope Leo XIV’s encyclical Magnifica Humanitas . This position will play an important role in thoughtfully implementing USD’s approach to AI in a way that aligns with our mission, vision, and values, and serves our entire community, especially students, faculty, and staff. Key responsibilities include: Clarity & Guidance: Support the development of institutional guidance and policy on the responsible use of AI in teaching, learning, and administrative practice, and collaborate with faculty, General Counsel, HR, and University Senate as appropriate. Foster Ongoing Dialogue: Collaborate with campus partners to organize speakers and support department- and unit-level conversations that advance campus-wide dialogue on AI. Ensuring Mission Alignment: Support the assessment of enterprise AI tools and resources, and contribute to institutional reporting that tracks USD's progress on AI initiatives. Incentivize Ideation: Contribute to the design and administration of internal grant programs that support faculty and staff exploration of AI, and encourage faculty-student research partnerships to examine the implications of AI within their disciplines. The Provost's Faculty Fellows reports directly to and works under the general supervision of the Associate Provost for Research and Administration. The appointment will start as soon as November 15, 2026. This position is renewable on an annual basis for up to two years. Each Faculty Fellow will serve an estimated one month in the summer, with a teaching load of one 3-unit course within their respective departments per each Fall and Spring semester. Each Faculty Fellow is expected to remain active in their ongoing faculty research and scholarship agenda. Job Requirements: Full-time faculty at USD. Strong familiarity with the university's academic and administrative structures. “Institutional-mindedness” as well as demonstrated trust and credibility among colleagues across the university. This position requires clear familiarity with AI tools and techniques alongside institutional judgment, trust, and the ability to work alongside others to move initiatives forward. Additionally, note that given the expectations required of this role including continued scholarship and teaching responsibilities, it is expected that the fellow will not engage in outside employment or consulting for the duration of the appointment. Special Application Instructions: Click the \"Apply Now\" button to complete our online application. In addition, please upload a cover letter and CV to your application profile for the hiring managers’ review. Review of applications will begin immediately with a priority deadline of November 15, 2026 . Note, however, that the job posting will be up for at least three days. After that time, applications will be reviewed by the hiring manager/committee throughout the posting period. A candidate may be selected at any time which could then close this posting on a date earlier than listed. Contact: Dr. Austin Choi-Fitzpatrick, caustin@sandiego.edu If you have any technical difficulties, please contact the Employment Services Team at jobs@sandiego.edu Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 635d928e Last Name (required) c83f83b7 Email (required) 63a60f73 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Senior Program Coordinator, Carnegie Elective Classification for Community Engagement San Diego, California School of Leadership and Education Sciences, Staff The University of San Diego, School of Leadership and Education Sciences (SOLES), in partnership with the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, hosts the long-established Carnegie Elective Classification for Community Engagement. The Community Engagement Classification serves as the leading framework for higher education community engagement work and is widely used to establish benchmarks and criteria for effectively institutionalizing community engagement across diverse institutional contexts. The Senior Program Coordinator provides essential administrative, logistical, and front-line support that keeps the classification's day-to-day operations running smoothly. Financial Aid Assistant, Military and Veteran Support San Diego, California Office of Financial Aid, Staff Financial Aid Assistant will coordinate VA/YR Scholarship Awards, Military Tuition Awards, ROTC Scholarships. Program Assistant - Professional and Continuing Education San Diego, California Continuing Education, Staff The Program Assistant provides essential administrative, operational, and customer service support for educational programs within Professional and Continuing Education (PCE). This role serves as a primary point of contact for students, prospective students, instructors, and external partners, ensuring smooth course administration, record management, and program logistics. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert eee171e9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Expression of Interest Faculty Office of the Vice President and Provost Expression of Interest Faculty Office of the Vice President and Provost Employment Type Faculty Full-time regular Faculty Full-time regular Locations San Diego, California, United States San Diego, California, United States First Name (required) 3bf1a709 Last Name (required) 96b2750f Email (required) a99b5f4d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook LinkedIn Instagram X © 2026 University of San Diego. All rights reserved. Cookie Preferences Web Privacy Web Accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
